Evelyn, Ted,<br />
<br />
We have it.<br />
<br />
The search ran in fourteen minutes yesterday afternoon - the archive platfo=
rm's year-end processing freeze pushed the run past the holidays - and the =
review finished this morning; the full report is attached with the recovere=
d messages and attachments as exhibits. The archive holds the complete elev=
en-message 2011 matter sequence, intact, with every attachment.<br />
<br />
The center of it is a June 9, 2011 email from Rosalind Tenniel to Arthur Pe=
llum, copying Walt Hagerman, with a signed letter on Torvane letterhead att=
ached. It confirms in terms that the engagement under 2011-0284 is limited =
to the Ridgeline claims; that Torvane considered the Brandt Thermal warrant=
y claim and elected not to assert it; that the claim is - her words - "expr=
essly outside the scope of your engagement," with the firm asked to take no=
 step to evaluate, preserve, or pursue it; that Torvane was advised of the =
limitations consequences and accepts them; and that the confirmation stands=
 unless she withdraws it in writing.<br />
<br />
The sequence around it is just as good: Wisner's May 17 limitations memo, A=
rthur's May 19 email recommending a tolling agreement, Tenniel's May 26 ema=
il about the sole-source relationship, Arthur's June 8 call memo, and his J=
une 10 instruction closing the tickler "per client written instruction." Th=
e file does not just contain the defense; it shows the firm gave exactly th=
e advice the demand letter says we never gave.<br />
<br />
Chain of custody note for whatever comes next: these are journal captures m=
ade at transmission in 2011, hash-verified on export. I have locked the exp=
ort set.<br />
<br />
Howell
